miting SSP price flexibility; 4. High working capital utilization (84%) and low cash balance (INR 0.8M); 5. Geopolitical disruption in West Asia affecting raw material supply.","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"n/a (non-concall source)","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"Despite negative EBITDA in prior years, KCFL's profitability in 9MFY26 was driven by a one-time subsidy jump (NBS increased from INR 5,122 to INR 8,149/ton), masking structural cost issues; sulphuric acid margins are a hidden bright spot but too small to offset SSP losses.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"},{"body":"- Maintains a healthy balance sheet with low long-term debt; net debt to equity improved from 1.4x in FY24 to 1.0x in FY26.\n- Capital allocation philosophy focuses on financial discipline to strengthen the balance sheet and build a foundation for sustainable long-term growth.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"SSP: 88% of revenue (FY25), 1.13 mtpa capacity, 44% utilization in 9MFY26; Sulphuric Acid: 11% of revenue, EBITDA/ton rose to INR 3,852 in 9MFY26 from INR 2,068 in FY25; by-product steam powers 4.32MW unit.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"},{"body":"- Holds ~10% share of India's SSP market, making it the second-largest producer nationally with over 40 years of industry presence.\n- Markets SSP under trusted umbrella brands 'Khaitan' and 'Utsav', supported by a network of 3,000+ dealers and 30,000+ retailers across 19 states.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Industry Leadership] Chairman Mr. Shailesh Khaitan serves on the FAI board and chaired the SSP Advisory Committee (2009–2023), providing policy-level influence in the fertilizer sector.\n- [Regulatory Tailwind] Kharif 2026 nutrient subsidy rates increased ~10% for N, P, and S vs. Rabi 2025, and freight subsidy for SSP continued, supporting affordability and demand.\n- [Soya Business Exit] Soya processing operations at Ratlam and Tri-Star were discontinued in 2012 due to declining profitability; significant land retained, and a discontinued operations loss of INR 42 Mn was recognized in FY26.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"SSP gross margin: negative under current subsidy (INR 8,149/ton) vs. cost of INR 15,500–16,500/ton (raw material + manufacturing); SA margin improved significantly due to higher realized prices and lower input costs relative to SSP.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Outlook hinges on ability to raise SSP retail prices without losing volume, consistent raw material supply, and timely subsidy releases; no formal guidance issued beyond monitoring these factors.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance / outlook"},{"body":"Not disclosed; sales volume for SSP was 0.38 mt in 9MFY26, up from 0.34 mt in FY24, but production halted at three plants due to cost constraints.","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"None identified; expansion constrained by capital intensity, subsidy dependency, and raw material volatility; potential upside only if SSP pricing power is restored and sulphur costs stabilize.","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (24-04-2026)","credit-rating action (India Ratings and Research (Ind-Ra) 24-04-2026)"],"thesis":"Khaitan Chemicals faces severe margin pressure on its core SSP business due to soaring sulphur prices and capped retail pricing, despite improved EBITDA from sulphuric acid and subsidy hikes; liquidity remains fragile with thin cash balances and high working capital dependency, making its financial stability contingent on timely subsidy disbursement and ability to pass on costs.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":1.05,"fy":"FY26","mcap":518,"opm":11.3,"pe":8.0,"roe":25.4}],"wtt":null},"meta":{"co":"KHAITAN CHEM & FERT LTD","isin":"INE745B01028","s":"KHAICHEM","sector":"Chemicals"},"s":"KHAICHEM"}